# Slice 346 (the book, forms-declare-or-call: the place may be declared anywhere in the method, in its var too): in
# the body of g the formal a and the own field n are known places of an int. The form `n: a + 1` on the own field is
# refused (8) when the call reaches it; the statement before it has run (calls is 1 in the graph), the return has not.
fn: g (int: a) int (int: calls 0; int: n 0)
    calls := calls + 1
    n: a + 1
    return: n
end: g
int: r g(1)
